## What it does

Simulates a few hundred price paths with geometric Brownian motion (standard library only),
summarises them with the numbers a quant looks at first (expected final price, Sharpe ratio and
maximum drawdown of the median path) and writes a self-contained HTML dashboard.

This project was created with the Quant Workbench (`qw new`); it follows the conventions of the
portfolio: parameters in `config/`, one module per concern in `src/`, results in `outputs/`.

